Here and below:

- the amplitude of AC signal at an oscilloscope channel is defined as the difference between the maximum and minimum of the signal. The corresponding function on the oscilloscope interface is «Vp-p»;
- for those experimental dependencies which ARE NOT supposed to be fitted with a linear function, it would be enough to obtain 12 experimental points uniformly distributed over the range under study;
- for those experimental dependencies which ARE supposed to be fitted with a linear function, it would be enough to obtain 7 experimental points uniformly distributed over the range under study.
